"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2863,"Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya, narrated to us Abu al-Nu'man, narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Kathir ibn Shinthir, on the authority of 'Ata', who said:

The beginning of the hastening (*idha'*) was from the Bedouins. They would stand at the sides of the people, having hung up their saddles, staffs, and cloaks. When the people would start to move (*ifadha*), they would start clattering and rattling, scaring the people. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was seen, and indeed the tips of his camel's hooves were touching the ground sharply as he was saying:

*""O people, upon you is tranquility! O people, upon you is tranquility!""*

And he would sometimes mention it from Ibn 'Abbas.

---

**CHAPTER:**"
